<title>POLAND: NFI units not to be traded on OTC market.</title>
<headline>NFI units not to be traded on OTC market.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of CeTO, the company controlling the CTO over-the-counter market, has decided to remove on July 19 Polish National Investment Fund (NFI) units from the registry of securities traded off-bourse, CeTO said.</p>
<p>&quot;CeTO's board has decided to remove on July 19 Polish National Investment Fund units from the registry of securities traded by CeTO,&quot; the company said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>The bourse and the Polish Securities Commission have long opposed simultaneous trading of the same instruments on and off-bourse.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
